options.explanation:
We need to convert square centimeters to square millimeters.

Since $1\,\text{centimeter}=10\,\text{millimeters}$, we know that both $\dfrac{1\,\text{centimeter}}{10\,\text{millimeters}}$ and $\dfrac{10\,\text{millimeters}}{1\,\text{centimeter}}$ equal $1$.

So we can multiply by either of those fractions to help us convert units, since multiplying by $1$ doesn't change value. In this problem, we multiply by $\left(\blueD{\dfrac{1\,\text{centimeter}}{10\,\text{millimeter}}}\right)^2$ since the rate we want to convert uses $\text{centimeters}^2$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}4500\,\dfrac{\text{bacteria}}{\text{centimeter}^2}\cdot \left(\blueD{\dfrac{1\,\text{centimeter}}{10\,\text{millimeter}}}\right)^2
\\\\
&=4500\,\dfrac{\text{bacteria}}{\cancel{\text{centimeter}^2}}\cdot \blueD{\dfrac{1\,\cancel{\text{centimeter}^2}}{100\,\text{millimeter}^2}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{4500}{100}\,\dfrac{\text{bacteria}}{\text{millimeter}^2}
\end{align}$
